* Magnifier — CESHAD shader agent (classifier 2 21 42001).
*
* PICK IT UP and it shrinks to carry size; DROP it in the world and it grows
* back. Dropped into the inventory drawer it STAYS small — that is what fits:
* the vehicle cabin check (AgentManager.cpp) rejects any agent wider or taller
* than the cabin. Pickup/drop is the trigger rather than a click, because a
* click on a carryable agent is taken by the Hand as a pick-up, so activate 1
* never arrives.
*
* The shrink is done by the SHADER: the lens radius (param 1) is eased down
* while the agent stays on the full 256x256 frame, so the lens closes smoothly.
* SHDR params interpolate in the engine (DrawableObject holds a target and the
* draw bracket eases toward it), so setting a new value animates it.
*
* Radius is in PIXELS, not sprite-UV, so the same value means the same
* on-screen lens on either frame. That is what lets the frame swap happen with
* NO shader change at all — no detach/re-attach, so no frame of the bare black
* surrogate showing through.
*
* PUHL gives each pose its own carry handle (the point the Hand holds it by),
* both at the frame's centre, so the hold point does not jump when the frame
* swaps. While carried the CARRIER owns the position, so the script must not
* mvto — it only re-centres when the swap happens in the world.
*
* NB: CAOS comments must be on their OWN line — a trailing "*" comment after a
* command silently aborts the rest of the script.
new: simp 2 21 42001 "magnifier" 2 0 8999
* attr 3 = carryable(1) + mouseable(2)
attr 3
bhvr 0
* carry handle at the centre of each frame
puhl 0 128 128
puhl 1 48 48
shdr "magnifier" { 2.0 108 0.01 0.004 }
* ov00: 0 = full size, 1 = carry size
setv ov00 0
* place it centred on the cursor
seta va10 targ
targ pntr
setv va00 posl
setv va01 post
targ va10
subv va00 128
subv va01 128
mvto va00 va01

* Picked up (script 4): ease the lens closed, then swap frame. No mvto — the
* carrier positions us, and PUHL keeps the hold point at the frame centre.
scrp 2 21 42001 4
  doif ov00 eq 0
    shdr "magnifier" { 3.0 40 0.012 0.006 }
    wait 14
    pose 1
    setv ov00 1
  endi
endm

* Dropped (script 5): in a vehicle (the drawer) it stays small. In the world it
* grows back — re-centred, since a frame swap is anchored top-left.
scrp 2 21 42001 5
  wait 3
  doif carr eq null
    doif ov00 eq 1
      pose 0
      setv va00 posl
      setv va01 post
      subv va00 80
      subv va01 80
      mvto va00 va01
      shdr "magnifier" { 2.0 108 0.01 0.004 }
      setv ov00 0
    endi
  endi
endm

* Re-attach the shader after a world load (a shdr attachment is not serialised).
scrp 2 21 42001 128
  doif ov00 eq 1
    shdr "magnifier" { 3.0 40 0.012 0.006 }
  else
    shdr "magnifier" { 2.0 108 0.01 0.004 }
  endi
endm
